        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "4 Bedroom Detached Bungalow | Approx. 0.7 Acre Site | Outbuilding / Shed | Generous Living Accommodation | BER D2\n\nLiam Reilly Auctioneers are delighted to present to the market this spacious four-bedroom detached bungalow, superbly positioned on a generous site extending to approximately 0.7 acres at Brownstown, Kilcloon, Co. Meath.\n\nSet back from the road behind a gated entrance and approached by a large driveway providing ample off-street parking, this attractive family home offers an excellent combination of generous accommodation, extensive gardens, useful outbuildings and a highly convenient countryside location.\n\nInternally, the property is bright and well proportioned, with extensive timber flooring running through much of the ground-floor accommodation. The welcoming entrance hall leads through to a particularly impressive open-plan kitchen, dining and family area, which forms the heart of the home.\n\nThe kitchen itself is generously sized and fitted with an extensive range of timber wall and floor units, tiled flooring and ample worktop and storage space. This opens into a substantial adjoining living/dining area featuring attractive exposed timber beams and posts, timber flooring, a built-in bar/breakfast counter and a feature brick fireplace with solid-fuel stove. Large windows provide plenty of natural light and pleasant views towards the surrounding gardens.\n\nA separate reception room provides a more formal living space and is a particularly bright and inviting room, with timber flooring, dual-aspect windows and an attractive feature fireplace.\n\nThe bedroom accommodation is equally well presented, with four bedrooms providing flexibility for family living, guest accommodation or home-office use. \n\nSeveral rooms benefit from fitted wardrobes and timber flooring. The family bathroom has been modernised with contemporary large-format wall tiling, tiled flooring, shower area, wash-hand basin, WC and heated towel rail.\n\nA further noteworthy feature is the converted attic space, accessed by a staircase from the main residence. The attic provides two spacious rooms, offering excellent additional accommodation and flexibility for a variety of uses, including home office space, a playroom or additional storage. This is a particularly useful addition to the property and complements the already generous accommodation available throughout the home.\n\nOutside\nThe property occupies an excellent site of approximately 0.7 acres, giving a wonderful sense of space around the residence.\n\nThe house is approached through a gated entrance onto a substantial driveway with extensive parking. Mature lawns, established trees, hedging and planting surround the property and create an attractive countryside setting.\n\nA detached outbuilding / shed is also included, providing valuable additional storage and adding considerably to the practicality of the property.\n\nThe combination of the generous site, detached bungalow accommodation and substantial outside space makes Brownstown an excellent option for families looking to enjoy country living while remaining within convenient commuting distance of Dublin and the surrounding towns.\n\nLocation\nBrownstown is situated in the Kilcloon area of County Meath, an attractive and highly regarded rural location close to the Kildare and Dublin borders.\n\nThe property enjoys the peace and space associated with countryside living while remaining within convenient reach of Kilcloon, Maynooth, Kilcock and Dunboyne. Maynooth in particular provides an extensive range of shopping, schools, cafés, restaurants, sporting facilities and everyday services, together with excellent public transport connections.\n\nKilcloon itself is well known for its strong local community, with primary school, church, sporting and community facilities serving the surrounding area.\n\nFor commuters, the location provides convenient access towards both the M4 and M3 motorway networks, while rail and bus connections are available from nearby towns, making the property an attractive option for those commuting to Dublin while seeking the benefits of a more spacious rural setting.\n\nFeatures\n•Spacious four-bedroom detached bungalow \n•Site extending to approximately 0.7 acres \n•Gated entrance and extensive off-street parking \n•Generous open-plan kitchen, dining and family accommodation \n•Large, fitted timber kitchen with excellent storage \n•Separate bright reception room \n•Feature fireplaces and solid-fuel stove \n•Attractive exposed timber beams and detailing \n•Extensive timber flooring \n•Four well-proportioned bedrooms \n•Modern family bathroom \n•Additional accommodation/storage at attic level \n•Large, mature gardens \n•Detached outbuilding / shed \n•Peaceful countryside setting \n•Convenient to Kilcloon, Maynooth, Kilcock and Dunboyne \n•Excellent accessibility to the M4 and M3 \n•BER: D2 \n•Eircode: A85 HY28 \n\n\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment with Liam Reilly Auctioneers.\n\nLIAM REILLY AUCTIONEERS give notice that; All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for the use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them.\n\n"
      },
